{"content":[{"text":"The text mesh (likely extruded from a Text object) got flipped — you're viewing the back face of the sign geometry, or the object/its text has a mirrored/negative scale on one axis.\n\nQuick things to check:\n\n1. **Negative scale**: select the sign/text object, open the N-panel — if Scale X (or Z) is `-1`, that's it. Select it and `Ctrl+A` → Apply → Scale won't fix mirroring by itself, but you'd want to fix the actual scale value or apply a Mirror modifier correctly instead of hand-flipping scale.\n2. **You're looking at the back of the text extrusion**: if it's a Text object extruded/converted to mesh, check if you're viewing it from behind (i.e., the gate's \"front\" in your scene is actually facing away from camera, so you're seeing the backside of a one-sided extrusion). Flip around to the other side and see if it reads correctly there — if so, just rotate the object/text 180° on its up axis instead of mirroring it.\n3. **Mirror modifier**: if this text is duplicated/mirrored from another sign (e.g. mirrored for a symmetric gate), check for a Mirror modifier with the wrong axis enabled.\n\nGiven it's mirrored left-right *and* upside-down (classic 180° rotation look, not just a flip), my best guess is **#2** — you're seeing the back of the arch from inside the park looking out, and the text was authored to face the other direction. Try orbiting to the opposite side of the gate.","type":"output_text"}],"event_id":"01a07e76-244b-7e51-ae35-054c5f378cc3:12","role":"assistant","session_id":"01a07e76-244b-7e51-ae35-054c5f378cc3","source_line":12,"timestamp":"2026-09-08T00:41:06.916Z","type":"message"}
